# ── dependencies ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/

# ── build outputs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The .vsix this repo produces, and the two entry files the bundlers WRITE
# (`tools/bundle-react.mjs`, `tools/bundle-xterm.mjs` regenerate them from
# nothing on every run, so they are build inputs, not sources).
*.vsix
tools/react-entry.js
tools/xterm-entry.js

# A TypeScript/other build dir, if someone adds one.
out/

# `npm pack` output — the upstream ships a tarball, so one sometimes lands in
# `hud/`.
*.tgz

# ── the VS Code test CLI ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode-test/

# ── secrets ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Two files that this project specifically must never carry:
#
#   `.env`               credential layer 4 is `<cwd>/.env` (see README §8), so a
#                        developer's own keys land exactly here;
#   `.credentials.yaml`  a copy of the DeepSeek Harness credential document,
#                        which is the thing layer 2 reads.
#
# `.env.example` is deliberately NOT ignored: a template with the variable NAMES
# is documentation, and the point of this block is values, not names.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.credentials.yaml
*.credentials.yaml

# A scratch DSH home pointed INSIDE the repo (the probes take `--home <dir>`) —
# it holds `storages/` and, if you put one there, a credential document.
.dsh/

# ── editor and OS noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/*
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# ── scratch scripts ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One-off probes are written as `tools/_<something>.mjs` and deleted when they
# have answered their question. Ignoring the convention means a forgotten one
# cannot be committed by accident.
tools/_*.mjs

# ── deliberately NOT ignored ───────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   media/react.js, media/xterm.js, media/theme.css
#       Generated by `npm run vendor` — and COMMITTED anyway, for exactly the
#       reason the upstream gives for committing its own `client.js`: they are
#       the artifacts the extension loads, the tests read them, and a checkout
#       that cannot be packaged without running a bundler is a checkout that
#       breaks the moment a bundler version drifts. `npm run verify` keeps them
#       honest instead.
#
#   hud/**
#       The upstream plugin, shipped byte for byte. It is not a dependency to be
#       installed — it IS the code under test, and `npm run check:verbatim`
#       compares the committed copy against the upstream checkout. Its own dev
#       artifacts (`hud/tools/vendor/`, `hud/tools/node_modules/`) are ignored by
#       `hud/.gitignore`, which came with the tree and travels with it.
#
#   package-lock.json
#       Committed on purpose: the extension ships `yaml` and `ssh2` as real
#       runtime dependencies, so the resolved tree is part of the release.
#
#   .vscodeignore
#       Not a variant of this file — it decides what goes INTO the .vsix.